othesis may only partially hold: some jailbreaks (e.g., adversarial suffixes) may work by other mechanisms (attention hijacking, refusal-action suppression) rather than lexical stripping, so Semantic-Recompute may help less on those. 4) Subtracting the lexical component could remove legitimate safety signal for prompts that are harmful precisely because of explicit content, causing new under-refusals; the Pareto sweep quantifies this. 5) A single harmfulness direction may be multi-dimensional; may require subspace projection. 6) Directions, lexical projections, and settings are model-specific and require per-model calibration. 7) Adaptive attackers targeting semantic encoding remain a threat, though this raises attack cost, itself a safety gain."}

