olding content fixed is delicate; residual confounds (topic, wording) could contaminate the direction. 3) Some jailbreaks (e.g., pure refusal-action suppression via abliteration) may NOT collapse verdict uncertainty, so VUR may help less on those; the per-direction shift analysis quantifies which attacks the mechanism explains. 4) 'Confidence is Not Competence' warns that decodable belief axes can be causally inert; verdict-uncertainty might likewise be non-actionable — the patching experiment is the crucial causal test, and a negative result is itself informative. 5) Re-injecting uncertainty could over-hedge and reduce helpfulness on legitimately confident benign requests; belief-gating and the Pareto sweep quantify this. 6) A single verdict-uncertainty direction may be multi-dimensional, requiring subspace re-injection. 7) Directions and gains are model-specific and need per-model calibration; adaptive attackers co-suppressing both axes remain a threat, though this raises attack cost."}
